WEBVTT

00:11.470 --> 00:17.480
(Episode 10:
Clover's Back in Action!)

00:22.840 --> 00:24.280
This feels great!

00:24.810 --> 00:27.529
If you're gonna climb up there,
be careful you don't fall.

00:27.530 --> 00:29.619
It's so much fun, too!

00:29.620 --> 00:32.290
I'm so excited to be going
to Duna with all of you!

00:32.630 --> 00:35.079
Marina, this isn't a game.

00:35.080 --> 00:36.419
It's a mission.

00:36.420 --> 00:38.399
I know that...

00:38.400 --> 00:41.009
But it's still exciting!

00:41.010 --> 00:43.419
Both the mission to explore a new dungeon

00:43.420 --> 00:45.639
and the two-week journey to Duna!

00:45.640 --> 00:46.929
You guys agree, don't you?

00:46.930 --> 00:49.399
Well, I mean...

00:49.400 --> 00:51.680
To be honest, I'm super hyped!

00:52.010 --> 00:54.769
You think the artifact bazaar
will be there?

00:54.770 --> 00:56.129
I'm not sure.

00:56.130 --> 00:58.529
Salmutaria, the nation that borders Duna,

00:58.530 --> 01:00.779
is particularly big on alchemy.

01:00.780 --> 01:04.439
They may be importing the
latest artifacts from there.

01:04.440 --> 01:07.950
Really? Now I'm getting
kind of excited, too.

01:08.190 --> 01:11.109
Yeah! As long as we're going,
let's enjoy it!

01:11.110 --> 01:14.330
A city I've never been
to and a new dungeon...

01:14.670 --> 01:16.420
I wonder what's waiting there!

01:28.090 --> 01:35.060
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:50.010 --> 02:51.339
(Duna, the Trade City)
(Finis, the Adventure City)

02:51.340 --> 02:57.520
(Finis, the Adventure City)

02:59.770 --> 03:02.770
(Finis, the Adventure City)

03:04.770 --> 03:07.280
(Finis, the Adventure City)

03:09.530 --> 03:11.990
(Finis, the Adventure City)

03:15.990 --> 03:17.990
(Duna, the Trade City)

03:22.000 --> 03:24.500
(Duna, the Trade City)

03:26.750 --> 03:28.760
(Duna, the Trade City)

03:30.760 --> 03:33.220
(Duna, the Trade City)

03:34.970 --> 03:37.470
(Duna, the Trade City)

03:45.190 --> 03:47.539
Wow, what a lively place!

03:47.540 --> 03:48.520
What's going on?

03:49.120 --> 03:51.279
Yuke, is that a restaurant?

03:51.280 --> 03:54.780
That's... a Salmutarian café, I think.

03:55.280 --> 03:57.530
Wow! What do they serve there?

03:57.880 --> 04:00.839
Well, Salmutaria's specialty
would be... let's see...

04:00.840 --> 04:02.889
Three-eyed Frog liver,
dripping with blood,

04:02.890 --> 04:05.309
served with Madara Swamp slugs
so fresh, they're still squirming...

04:05.310 --> 04:06.040
Ugh...

04:06.670 --> 04:10.209
I'm kidding. It's real, decent food.

04:10.210 --> 04:12.219
Want to go check it out
while we're in town?

04:12.220 --> 04:13.799
Yeah! I can't wait!

04:13.800 --> 04:16.079
We'll look for artifacts
while we're at it.

04:16.080 --> 04:16.930
Yeah.

04:17.200 --> 04:20.159
Looks like there are a lot
of stalls and food places.

04:20.160 --> 04:22.329
They do call this the Trade City.

04:22.330 --> 04:25.579
We might get to try rare foods
we've never seen before.

04:25.580 --> 04:28.690
You're quite the gourmand, after all.

04:29.030 --> 04:31.690
I mean, nothing beats good food, right?

04:32.070 --> 04:33.950
There are a lot of adventurers.

04:34.400 --> 04:37.879
Word of the new dungeon
must have gotten around.

04:37.880 --> 04:40.799
Looks like there are even
some from other countries.

04:40.800 --> 04:41.950
You can tell?

04:42.400 --> 04:44.710
See how some of them
are dressed differently?

04:45.000 --> 04:48.339
Those cloaks are Salmutarian attire.

04:48.340 --> 04:50.249
The patterns and colors have meaning.

04:50.250 --> 04:52.459
They tell you what areas
and families they come from.

04:52.460 --> 04:53.879
Oh, I get it.

04:53.880 --> 04:55.470
They're really pretty cloaks!

04:55.960 --> 05:00.409
Salmutaria is a nation with very
strong feudalistic tendencies,

05:00.410 --> 05:03.220
so hierarchies and lineages
are really important to them.

05:03.770 --> 05:06.679
The jobs they're allowed to take
depend on their social status,

05:06.680 --> 05:09.729
and it's all managed by
individual households.

05:09.730 --> 05:12.459
So those people back there were a family?

05:12.460 --> 05:15.719
They were wearing kilts with the
same pattern, so yeah, probably.

05:15.720 --> 05:18.629
Those kilts were so pretty.

05:18.630 --> 05:20.240
I wonder where they sell them...

05:20.660 --> 05:23.059
Could we make things like that
for ourselves?

05:23.060 --> 05:24.000
Things like what?

05:24.280 --> 05:26.869
Matching cloaks and armbands and stuff!

05:26.870 --> 05:29.579
That might be a good idea.

05:29.580 --> 05:30.880
Yeah. Matching.

05:31.220 --> 05:32.999
Oh, yeah... Good point.

05:33.000 --> 05:35.309
Something like that might be good to have.

05:35.310 --> 05:36.859
I'll think of something.

05:36.860 --> 05:37.839
Yay!

05:37.840 --> 05:39.189
I look forward to it!

05:39.190 --> 05:40.140
Me, too.

05:40.610 --> 05:43.269
Let's see... Since we have the chance,

05:43.270 --> 05:47.329
I could use alchemy to add some magical
effect to them, making them artifacts,

05:47.330 --> 05:49.419
so they'll have a practical use...

05:49.420 --> 05:51.909
Yuke's cooking up some plot again.

05:51.910 --> 05:54.150
Huh? Ah... I couldn't help myself.

05:54.520 --> 05:56.900
I can see the Adventurer's Guild!

06:01.120 --> 06:03.620
(Duna Adventurer's Guild)

06:08.280 --> 06:10.639
Silk and I will go meet
with the guild master.

06:10.640 --> 06:12.519
The rest of you can relax at the pub.

06:12.520 --> 06:14.000
Okay. And...

06:14.330 --> 06:16.130
We'll gather some intel, too!

06:16.440 --> 06:20.839
Right. The rumors and chatter you hear
in pubs can be surprisingly useful.

06:20.840 --> 06:22.049
We're on it.

06:22.050 --> 06:24.149
Don't get too carried away.

06:24.150 --> 06:25.209
Well, let's go.

06:25.210 --> 06:26.140
Right.

06:33.000 --> 06:34.689
I'm Guild Master Maniella.

06:34.690 --> 06:35.049
(Duna Adventurers' Guild )
(Guild Master Maniella)
I'm Guild Master Maniella.

06:35.050 --> 06:36.900
Good to meet you.
(Duna Adventurers' Guild )
(Guild Master Maniella)

06:37.200 --> 06:41.759
I'm Yuke Feldio, leader of
the C-rank party Clover.

06:41.760 --> 06:44.749
I'm its subleader, Silk Amberwood.

06:44.750 --> 06:46.289
It's a pleasure to meet you.

06:46.290 --> 06:49.339
I love to see young people
with proper manners.

06:49.340 --> 06:52.040
Got the details of the quest
in your heads already?

06:52.410 --> 06:54.540
Benwood has given us the gist of it.

06:54.890 --> 06:57.939
There are a few additional
details we'd like to confirm.

06:57.940 --> 07:00.049
What shall we do in the way
of mapping the dungeon?

07:00.050 --> 07:03.959
You can if you want, but it's
not required for the job.

07:03.960 --> 07:07.679
We'll hear from people who make a living
doing that once the event's over.

07:07.680 --> 07:10.690
And regarding any items or
monster materials we find...

07:11.080 --> 07:13.639
Generally speaking, they're yours to keep.

07:13.640 --> 07:17.909
But we will check over everything
you bring back and put it on a list.

07:17.910 --> 07:20.450
Can't guarantee you won't find
anything dangerous, after all.

07:21.880 --> 07:25.830
Hey, now. Don't go shooting
appraising looks at your elders.

07:26.230 --> 07:29.159
Are you wondering how I could tell?

07:29.160 --> 07:31.249
Call it the wisdom of old age.

07:31.250 --> 07:35.840
That said, you're correct to be
wary of someone you've never met.

07:36.150 --> 07:40.590
Especially when you're leading a
bunch of beauties like this around.

07:42.100 --> 07:44.589
I apologize for my rude behavior.

07:44.590 --> 07:46.139
It's all good.

07:46.140 --> 07:49.600
Starting today, we'll be
business partners for a while.

07:49.900 --> 07:51.980
We oughta get along, right?

07:53.100 --> 07:56.110
So? When are you going in?

07:56.440 --> 07:57.770
Well...

08:00.370 --> 08:03.369
We'd like to recover from our
journey first, then prepare,

08:03.370 --> 08:05.109
and enter the dungeon in three days.

08:05.110 --> 08:06.939
Good decision.

08:06.940 --> 08:10.329
I can see why you're Benwood's favorites.

08:10.330 --> 08:11.000
Huh?

08:11.370 --> 08:14.179
Benwood and I go way back, you know.

08:14.180 --> 08:16.959
You really don't know who I am?

08:16.960 --> 08:20.279
I used to be a member of Anubis.

08:20.280 --> 08:20.759
What?!

08:20.760 --> 08:24.319
I was the first one to set
foot on the deepest level

08:24.320 --> 08:26.850
of Achromatic Darkness,
I'll have you know.

08:27.750 --> 08:32.020
In other words, your uncle,
Saga, was a buddy of mine.

08:33.890 --> 08:37.759
So let's see what you're made of, Yuke.

08:37.760 --> 08:40.429
P-Please be gentle with me...

08:40.430 --> 08:41.649
Also...

08:41.650 --> 08:42.620
Here.

08:46.320 --> 08:50.999
Your party came here for a mission.
Feels wrong to make you hunt for lodging.

08:51.000 --> 08:54.009
I had the guild arrange something for you.

08:54.010 --> 08:55.960
Just follow that map.

08:56.410 --> 08:59.639
Thank you for doing all this.

08:59.640 --> 09:00.960
Thank you!

09:13.410 --> 09:14.609
Were you nervous?

09:14.610 --> 09:15.980
Yes, extremely.

09:16.450 --> 09:21.189
It's just like you to be able to handle
a conversation like that so calmly.

09:21.190 --> 09:23.179
I was nervous, too.

09:23.180 --> 09:25.240
Her presence was just overwhelming.

09:25.530 --> 09:28.579
And she even arranged lodging for us.

09:28.580 --> 09:32.709
Since she went to the trouble,
we should gratefully accept the offer.

09:32.710 --> 09:35.250
It's a big help
since we don't know the city.

09:37.150 --> 09:39.449
(Salmutarian:) Why don't you pour us some wine?

09:39.450 --> 09:40.700
(Salmutarian:) Hurry up!

09:40.800 --> 09:45.020
(Salmutarian:) We are men, you know?

09:45.130 --> 09:48.119
I'll only say this one more time:
Get out of here!

09:48.120 --> 09:49.009
Right now!

09:49.010 --> 09:50.999
That's it! Fight them!

09:51.000 --> 09:53.140
You got this, girlies!

09:54.270 --> 09:55.140
What's going on, Marina?!

09:55.420 --> 09:57.520
Yuke! These guys are...

09:57.800 --> 10:00.369
(Salmutarian:) Hurry up, you're just women!

10:00.370 --> 10:04.800
(Salmutarian:)
You're women, after all, aren't you?

10:05.320 --> 10:07.149
They're speaking Salmutarian?

10:07.150 --> 10:10.179
They tried to force us
to pour their drinks!

10:10.180 --> 10:11.530
Oh...

10:11.980 --> 10:19.040
(Salmutarian:)
These women... are my... wives,
love... I love them every night.

10:23.240 --> 10:24.709
What did you say?

10:24.710 --> 10:28.029
"They're all my precious
family and companions."

10:28.030 --> 10:29.800
I think I got it right...

10:32.800 --> 10:34.639
Aw, it's over already?

10:34.640 --> 10:36.199
Let's get back to drinking.

10:36.200 --> 10:38.060
That was a fun little show.

10:38.440 --> 10:41.279
They could've stopped those guys
instead of just watching...

10:41.280 --> 10:42.310
Are you all right?

10:42.590 --> 10:46.079
Yeah. They tried to touch
my shoulder a little,

10:46.080 --> 10:48.269
but Rain saved me with her magic.

10:48.270 --> 10:51.629
I shouldn't have held back.

10:51.630 --> 10:53.479
Those bastards.

10:53.480 --> 10:56.449
I was this close to slicing their throats.

10:56.450 --> 10:59.710
Those guys should be thanking me, I guess.

11:02.550 --> 11:06.399
Salmutaria is a country where men
traditionally dominate women.

11:06.400 --> 11:08.999
In their homeland, women are only allowed

11:09.000 --> 11:11.759
to have children
and help with the housework.

11:11.760 --> 11:14.219
They're treated as human property.

11:14.220 --> 11:15.879
That's not right!

11:15.880 --> 11:17.180
It's too weird!

11:17.750 --> 11:22.449
I agree, but that's the kind
of country Salmutaria is.

11:22.450 --> 11:25.559
Why did they end up just leaving, then?

11:25.560 --> 11:27.959
That's a good question.

11:27.960 --> 11:32.700
If they saw us as assets, they
could have been more aggressive.

11:33.000 --> 11:36.949
In Salmutaria, religious belief
and the law are tied together.

11:36.950 --> 11:40.079
There are some very harsh
punishments for breaking the law.

11:40.080 --> 11:41.330
Such as?

11:41.720 --> 11:44.839
They're dealt punishment equal
to the crime they committed.

11:44.840 --> 11:48.340
If those guys had...
sorry to put it this way...

11:48.940 --> 11:52.059
If they'd taken you, my property,
away from me,

11:52.060 --> 11:56.220
they couldn't complain if their property was
taken from them in the name of their god.

11:56.470 --> 11:57.819
I get it!

11:57.820 --> 12:02.100
So you were asserting
your ownership of us?

12:02.420 --> 12:04.749
The nuance isn't quite the same, but yeah.

12:04.750 --> 12:08.389
I only studied Salmutarian
once a few years ago,

12:08.390 --> 12:10.860
but since they left,
I guess they got the message.

12:12.200 --> 12:13.669
What's up, Marina?

12:13.670 --> 12:17.239
Hey, Yuke! We really should
make matching gear!

12:17.240 --> 12:21.999
Then those guys will understand
that we belong to you, right?

12:22.000 --> 12:23.909
"Belong" to me?

12:23.910 --> 12:25.979
I get what you're saying,

12:25.980 --> 12:29.479
but I wish you wouldn't phrase it in
ways that will cause misunderstandings.

12:29.480 --> 12:32.260
I get it, though. I'll come up
with something as soon as I can.

12:34.530 --> 12:37.579
Hey, Yuke, can I say one thing?

12:37.580 --> 12:38.260
What?

12:38.760 --> 12:41.520
Your Salmutarian wasn't quite right.

12:41.840 --> 12:44.890
Huh? Then... what did I say?

12:46.200 --> 12:47.020
Rain?

12:54.030 --> 12:56.530
(The Singing Fawn)

12:56.830 --> 12:58.279
Hi there!

12:58.280 --> 13:00.529
Welcome to The Singing Fawn!

13:00.530 --> 13:02.819
I'm Fina, the owner.

13:02.820 --> 13:06.790
I'll be taking care of you for
the duration of your stay.

13:07.160 --> 13:08.869
I appreciate it.

13:08.870 --> 13:12.670
I'm Yuke Feldio, the leader of Clover.

13:12.960 --> 13:15.079
Yes, I know you.

13:15.080 --> 13:17.679
I'm actually a fan of Clover.

13:17.680 --> 13:20.409
Th-Thank you.

13:20.410 --> 13:22.480
This place is amazing.

13:23.180 --> 13:26.089
The spirits here are incredibly stable.

13:26.090 --> 13:29.159
I feel as if I'm in a forest sanctuary.

13:29.160 --> 13:30.309
I wonder why...

13:30.310 --> 13:32.189
It feels calming somehow.

13:32.190 --> 13:35.990
Doesn't it? I feel like
I'm just visiting family!

13:36.810 --> 13:39.729
I'm so happy to hear you say that.

13:39.730 --> 13:43.529
Oh, and all your needs will
be covered by the guild,

13:43.530 --> 13:45.509
so you don't need to pay for anything.

13:45.510 --> 13:47.079
Even meals?!

13:47.080 --> 13:52.539
Yes. You're welcome to eat as
much as you'd like, Marina.

13:52.540 --> 13:56.510
I saw how you ate in the
Achromatic Darkness stream.

13:57.410 --> 13:59.009
I'm so embarrassed!

13:59.010 --> 14:02.009
I gotta make sure Camerat doesn't
record me eating anymore...

14:02.010 --> 14:07.079
This inn is reserved for your party's
exclusive use during the mission period,

14:07.080 --> 14:09.319
so please make yourselves comfortable.

14:09.320 --> 14:11.019
Although it won't be for very long,

14:11.020 --> 14:14.969
I'll do my best to make
this place feel like home.

14:14.970 --> 14:16.280
It's reserved just for us?

14:16.760 --> 14:17.489
Yes.

14:17.490 --> 14:22.049
If you'll pardon my saying so, I assumed you
wouldn't want lots of other people around,

14:22.050 --> 14:24.290
so I took the liberty of
closing it to the public.

14:24.680 --> 14:27.319
Um... Thank you for that.

14:27.320 --> 14:31.040
I've never been here before,
so I did feel a bit concerned.

14:31.560 --> 14:33.540
Allow me to thank you, too.

14:33.860 --> 14:37.359
You can use whichever rooms
you like on the second floor.

14:37.360 --> 14:38.809
And...

14:38.810 --> 14:42.050
If you don't mind, I'd like to show
you this inn's main attraction.

14:42.540 --> 14:43.580
Main attraction?

14:46.680 --> 14:49.310
Is this... a rooftop garden?

14:51.080 --> 14:52.190
Wait, is this...

14:52.710 --> 14:53.940
a hot spring?!

14:54.240 --> 14:56.550
Yes, it certainly is.

14:58.850 --> 15:01.780
It can relieve your exhaustion, and
it's good for your skin, as well.

15:02.100 --> 15:03.279
A hot spring?

15:03.280 --> 15:05.469
So this is one of those?

15:05.470 --> 15:07.539
Nene, what is a hot spring?

15:07.540 --> 15:10.619
Well, um... it's like a bath.

15:10.620 --> 15:12.540
The hot water comes up from underground.

15:12.920 --> 15:16.519
Wouldn't hot water from
underground boil you alive?

15:16.520 --> 15:19.889
I guess there are some things
even you don't know, huh?

15:19.890 --> 15:21.429
What about the rest of you?

15:21.430 --> 15:23.239
I've never seen one.

15:23.240 --> 15:24.259
Same.

15:24.260 --> 15:26.059
I haven't, either.

15:26.060 --> 15:29.129
In that case,
we should all get in together!

15:29.130 --> 15:30.980
Then you won't feel afraid!

15:33.060 --> 15:35.440
Th-This feels so good.

15:35.800 --> 15:37.900
I'm in heaven.

15:38.440 --> 15:41.739
Gosh, did I just say "heaven"?

15:41.740 --> 15:44.819
It just spilled out so naturally.

15:44.820 --> 15:47.709
This is a hot spring! They're the best!

15:47.710 --> 15:49.330
It's pure bliss.

15:53.610 --> 15:56.340
An amazing hot spring
followed by a tasty meal...

15:56.760 --> 15:59.380
I wish I could live here forever!

15:59.750 --> 16:02.249
You know we can't do that.

16:02.250 --> 16:04.760
But I understand how you feel.

16:05.140 --> 16:07.390
It soaks into every fiber of your body!

16:08.720 --> 16:09.640
Delicious.

16:11.020 --> 16:13.879
Marina, would you care for seconds?

16:13.880 --> 16:15.309
Yes, please!

16:15.310 --> 16:16.100
Sure!

16:18.270 --> 16:20.280
(Two days later)

16:20.760 --> 16:23.399
We'll be entering
the new dungeon tomorrow,

16:23.400 --> 16:25.780
so we're holding this meeting
to go over some things.

16:26.280 --> 16:29.019
The dungeon Clover will be
visiting this time

16:29.020 --> 16:32.979
is the new dungeon that's been
discovered on the bank of Lake Ryne,

16:32.980 --> 16:34.160
near the trading city of Duna.

16:34.610 --> 16:39.129
The plan is to proceed as we did
when we visited Achromatic Darkness.

16:39.130 --> 16:43.419
We'll livestream the quest while attempting
to conquer as many floors as possible.

16:43.420 --> 16:46.919
That said, once we get as
far as the fifth floor,

16:46.920 --> 16:49.009
chances are good it'll
be opened to the public.

16:49.010 --> 16:51.679
So that will be our first goal.

16:51.680 --> 16:56.199
The only information we have now is that
the first floor is an underground waterway.

16:56.200 --> 16:57.709
The rest is unknown.

16:57.710 --> 16:59.629
Based on the location,

16:59.630 --> 17:01.689
its monsters are likely to be things like

17:01.690 --> 17:06.449
aquatic species, rats,
insects, and slimes.

17:06.450 --> 17:10.569
Also, this will be a race against
other parties to determine

17:10.570 --> 17:12.079
who can conquer the dungeon first.

17:12.080 --> 17:14.710
What are the other parties like?

17:15.120 --> 17:17.460
The ones chosen by the kingdom
to participate

17:17.790 --> 17:20.920
are Fullbound, a B-rank party from Duna...

17:21.190 --> 17:25.970
Misty, an up-and-coming B-rank
party from the capital...

17:26.690 --> 17:28.470
and our party, Clover.

17:29.060 --> 17:31.189
As far as the race is concerned...

17:31.190 --> 17:33.939
I'd like us to proceed without
even thinking about it.

17:33.940 --> 17:36.889
You mean we won't actively
participate in the race?

17:36.890 --> 17:37.989
Right.

17:37.990 --> 17:42.070
From our perspective, both other
parties are more experienced.

17:42.790 --> 17:46.019
If we overreach in an attempt to catch
up to them, someone could get hurt.

17:46.020 --> 17:49.820
We just need to be ourselves and
do our job like we always do.

17:50.110 --> 17:51.329
Right!

17:51.330 --> 17:53.179
Any questions so far?

17:53.180 --> 17:53.979
Me!

17:53.980 --> 17:55.079
Yes, Marina.

17:55.080 --> 17:58.210
How far are we hoping
to get on our first run?

17:58.490 --> 18:00.710
What kind of pace should we take?

18:01.220 --> 18:05.469
We'll prioritize reaching the stairs
to the second floor tomorrow,

18:05.470 --> 18:08.349
and do a broad investigation of
the first floor along the way.

18:08.350 --> 18:09.470
Broad?

18:09.800 --> 18:15.119
The first five floors need to be investigated
before it can be opened to the public,

18:15.120 --> 18:18.229
but we can figure out how expansive
and dangerous it is to, some extent,

18:18.230 --> 18:20.600
by how big the first floor is
and what monsters are on it.

18:21.000 --> 18:24.799
There may be more than one stairway
to the second floor, too,

18:24.800 --> 18:28.360
so we want as much information
on the first floor as we can get.

18:28.760 --> 18:31.739
So we should pace ourselves
for the long haul!

18:31.740 --> 18:34.059
Once we locate the area
where the stairs are,

18:34.060 --> 18:37.219
we'll have time to think
about our next steps.

18:37.220 --> 18:39.399
That's why finding the
stairs is our top priority.

18:39.400 --> 18:41.449
Right, just like always!

18:41.450 --> 18:42.380
And Nene...

18:42.770 --> 18:43.630
Yes!

18:44.060 --> 18:47.959
I don't think we'll be able to use
Wind Priming inside this dungeon.

18:47.960 --> 18:52.139
It's close to a lake, and when there's
flowing water nearby, it's less accurate.

18:52.140 --> 18:53.640
Understood.

18:53.940 --> 18:58.770
So I'd like you to handle the
advance precautions again.

18:59.350 --> 19:02.029
Roger! Just leave it to me!

19:02.030 --> 19:03.150
I'll nail it!

19:03.400 --> 19:04.449
Good.

19:04.450 --> 19:08.669
So today, focus on making preparations
and getting plenty of rest,

19:08.670 --> 19:10.279
so you're ready for tomorrow.

19:10.280 --> 19:11.410
Got it!

19:23.170 --> 19:26.210
(Lake Ryne)

19:31.660 --> 19:34.140
The big cottage over there
is the command center.

19:34.570 --> 19:38.299
People from the Royal Academy
are stationed there, too.

19:38.300 --> 19:42.020
I'll be watching from in there
while you guys are in the dungeon.

19:42.510 --> 19:44.770
Tablets actually work out here?

19:45.090 --> 19:49.719
Apparently, those scholar types brought
some artifact that makes them work.

19:49.720 --> 19:52.349
I don't really get that kinda stuff,

19:52.350 --> 19:54.160
but it sure makes things convenient.

19:54.470 --> 19:57.779
Hey, what's this dungeon called, anyway?

19:57.780 --> 20:01.079
It doesn't have a name yet since
we don't know what's in it.

20:01.080 --> 20:04.229
Oh... That's a little inconvenient.

20:04.230 --> 20:07.789
Well, you might turn out to be the
adventurers who get to name it.

20:07.790 --> 20:09.170
So do a good job!

20:09.690 --> 20:10.799
Name it?

20:10.800 --> 20:13.299
That's a tremendous honor!

20:13.300 --> 20:16.430
An adventurer couldn't ask for more!

20:16.820 --> 20:20.310
That'd be pretty cool, but we
can't push ourselves too hard.

20:20.800 --> 20:21.570
Right!

20:30.520 --> 20:33.279
It's been ages since we
were last in a dungeon!

20:33.280 --> 20:35.360
Work hard with Mom and Dad, okay?

20:35.640 --> 20:37.370
I'm a little nervous.

20:39.620 --> 20:42.250
Master, everything's ready.

20:42.630 --> 20:45.500
Okay, then, I'm starting up Camerat now.

20:47.750 --> 20:49.520
Beginning stream.

20:51.100 --> 20:53.479
Long time no see, everyone.

20:53.480 --> 20:54.260
This is Clover.

20:54.600 --> 20:56.259
Hey, it's Clover!

20:56.260 --> 20:57.919
I guess they're finally back!

20:57.920 --> 20:59.059
I've been waiting!

20:59.060 --> 21:01.390
Oh, where are they? What dungeon?

21:01.720 --> 21:04.640
We're here on a mission to check
out a new dungeon in Duna!

21:05.080 --> 21:07.649
This is our first quest in some time.
We'll do our best.

21:07.650 --> 21:11.829
Apparently, it's been over ten years
since a new dungeon was discovered!

21:11.830 --> 21:13.530
Be sure to cheer us on!

21:14.000 --> 21:16.839
Time for the first quest
since our comeback.

21:16.840 --> 21:18.280
Let's have fun, but be careful.

21:21.140 --> 21:22.290
Ready, set...

21:22.760 --> 21:24.830
Clover!

22:56.050 --> 22:57.039
(The Capital Distorted by the Twilight)

22:57.040 --> 22:59.739
Next time, "The Capital Distorted by the Twilight."

22:59.740 --> 23:01.050
(The Capital Distorted by the Twilight)
